<h1>Control Flow: Conditionals and Loops</h1>

<p><strong>Control flow</strong> refers to the order in which a program's instructions are executed. Without control flow, a program would simply execute every line from top to bottom in sequence. With control flow, a program can make decisions and repeat actions — which is what makes programs truly useful.</p>

<h2>Part 1: Conditional Statements</h2>

<h3>The if Statement</h3>
<p>An <code>if</code> statement executes a block of code only if a condition is <code>True</code>.</p>
<pre><code>score = 75

if score >= 50:
    print("You passed!")
</code></pre>
<p>The indented block (4 spaces) is the body of the <code>if</code> statement. Python uses indentation — not curly braces — to define blocks.</p>

<h3>The if-else Statement</h3>
<p>An <code>else</code> clause provides an alternative when the condition is <code>False</code>.</p>
<pre><code>score = 40

if score >= 50:
    print("You passed!")
else:
    print("You failed. Please try again.")
</code></pre>

<h3>The if-elif-else Statement</h3>
<p>Use <code>elif</code> (short for "else if") to check multiple conditions in sequence. Only the first matching block executes.</p>
<pre><code>score = 72

if score >= 70:
    grade = "A"
elif score >= 60:
    grade = "B"
elif score >= 50:
    grade = "C"
elif score >= 45:
    grade = "D"
else:
    grade = "F"

print(f"Your grade is: {grade}")   # Output: Your grade is: A
</code></pre>

<h2>Part 2: Comparison Operators</h2>
<p>Conditions are built using comparison operators that return <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Operator</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th><th>Result</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>==</code></td><td>Equal to</td><td><code>5 == 5</code></td><td>True</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>!=</code></td><td>Not equal to</td><td><code>5 != 3</code></td><td>True</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>&gt;</code></td><td>Greater than</td><td><code>7 &gt; 5</code></td><td>True</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>&lt;</code></td><td>Less than</td><td><code>3 &lt; 8</code></td><td>True</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>&gt;=</code></td><td>Greater than or equal</td><td><code>5 &gt;= 5</code></td><td>True</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>&lt;=</code></td><td>Less than or equal</td><td><code>4 &lt;= 6</code></td><td>True</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="highlight">
  <strong>Common mistake:</strong> Do not confuse <code>=</code> (assignment) with <code>==</code> (comparison). Writing <code>if x = 5:</code> is a syntax error in Python.
</div>

<h2>Part 3: Logical Operators</h2>
<p>Logical operators combine multiple conditions:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Operator</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th><th>Result</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>and</code></td><td>Both must be True</td><td><code>x &gt; 0 and x &lt; 10</code></td><td>True if x is between 0 and 10</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>or</code></td><td>At least one must be True</td><td><code>x == 0 or x == 1</code></td><td>True if x is 0 or 1</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>not</code></td><td>Reverses the boolean</td><td><code>not (x &gt; 5)</code></td><td>True if x is 5 or less</td></tr>
</table>

<pre><code>age = 22
has_id = True

if age >= 18 and has_id:
    print("Entry permitted.")
else:
    print("Entry denied.")
</code></pre>

<h2>Part 4: for Loops</h2>
<p>A <code>for</code> loop iterates over a sequence (list, string, range, etc.), executing the body once for each item.</p>

<h3>for loop with range()</h3>
<pre><code># Print numbers 1 through 5
for i in range(1, 6):
    print(i)
# Output: 1  2  3  4  5
</code></pre>
<p><code>range(start, stop)</code> generates integers from <code>start</code> up to (but not including) <code>stop</code>. <code>range(5)</code> gives 0, 1, 2, 3, 4.</p>

<h3>for loop over a list</h3>
<pre><code>courses = ["Physics", "Maths", "Economics", "Programming"]

for course in courses:
    print(f"Studying: {course}")
</code></pre>

<h3>for loop over a string</h3>
<pre><code>word = "NIGERIA"
for letter in word:
    print(letter)
# Output: N I G E R I A (each on a new line)
</code></pre>

<h3>Nested for loops</h3>
<pre><code># Multiplication table for 3
for i in range(1, 11):
    print(f"3 x {i} = {3 * i}")
</code></pre>

<h2>Part 5: while Loops</h2>
<p>A <code>while</code> loop repeats its body as long as a condition remains <code>True</code>.</p>
<pre><code>count = 1
while count <= 5:
    print(f"Count: {count}")
    count += 1     # IMPORTANT: update the counter or the loop never ends
print("Done!")
</code></pre>

<div class="highlight">
  <strong>Infinite Loop Warning:</strong> If the loop condition never becomes False, the program will run forever and hang. Always ensure the loop variable is updated inside the loop body.
</div>

<h3>while loop for input validation</h3>
<pre><code>password = ""
while password != "secret123":
    password = input("Enter the password: ")
print("Access granted!")
</code></pre>

<h2>Part 6: break and continue</h2>

<h3>break — exit the loop immediately</h3>
<pre><code>for i in range(1, 11):
    if i == 6:
        break          # Stop the loop when i reaches 6
    print(i)
# Output: 1 2 3 4 5
</code></pre>

<h3>continue — skip the current iteration and move to the next</h3>
<pre><code>for i in range(1, 11):
    if i % 2 == 0:
        continue       # Skip even numbers
    print(i)
# Output: 1 3 5 7 9
</code></pre>

<h2>Putting It All Together: Practical Example</h2>
<pre><code># Guess the number game
import random

secret = random.randint(1, 10)
attempts = 0
max_attempts = 3

print("Guess a number between 1 and 10. You have 3 tries.")

while attempts < max_attempts:
    guess = int(input("Your guess: "))
    attempts += 1

    if guess == secret:
        print(f"Correct! You got it in {attempts} attempt(s).")
        break
    elif guess < secret:
        print("Too low!")
    else:
        print("Too high!")
else:
    # The else clause of a while loop runs if the loop ended normally (no break)
    print(f"Sorry, the number was {secret}.")
</code></pre>

<div class="highlight">
  <strong>Key Points:</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><code>if/elif/else</code> — make decisions based on conditions</li>
    <li><code>for</code> — iterate a known number of times or over a collection</li>
    <li><code>while</code> — repeat while a condition holds</li>
    <li><code>break</code> — exit a loop early</li>
    <li><code>continue</code> — skip the rest of the current iteration</li>
    <li>Python uses <strong>indentation</strong> (4 spaces) to define code blocks — this is required, not optional</li>
  </ul>
</div>
<div id="live-file-panel" style="display:none;margin:20px 0;padding:16px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:6px;background:#f9f9f9;">
  <strong>Live File</strong>
  <div id="live-file-content" style="margin-top:8px;color:#555;"></div>
</div>
<script>
(function(){
  const parts = window.location.pathname.split('/').filter(Boolean);
  const apiBase = 'https://api.kenechukwuosele.me';
  let course = '', week = '';
  if(parts.length >= 3 && parts[0] === 'courses'){
    course = parts[1];
    week = parts[2];
  } else if(parts.length >= 2 && parts[0] !== 'courses'){
    course = parts[0];
    week = parts[1];
  } else {
    return;
  }
  course = course.trim();
  week = week.trim();
  if(!course || !week) return;
  const panel = document.getElementById('live-file-panel');
  const content = document.getElementById('live-file-content');
    function renderFile(meta){
    if(!meta){
      panel.style.display = 'none';
      return;
    }
    const url = apiBase + '/live-file/' + course + '/' + week;
    const dlUrl = url + '?download=1';
    const type = meta.content_type || '';
    const safeName = meta.filename || 'file';
    let html = '<div><a href="' + dlUrl + '" style="color:#2572F5;text-decoration:underline;cursor:pointer;">Download ' + safeName + '</a></div>';
    if(type.startsWith('image/')){
      fetch(url).then(r=>r.blob()).then(b=>{
        const el = document.getElementById('live-file-img');
        if(el) el.src = URL.createObjectURL(b);
      });
      html += '<div style="margin-top:10px;"><img id="live-file-img" src="" alt="' + safeName + '" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:4px;"/></div>';
    } else if(type === 'application/pdf'){
      fetch(url).then(r=>r.blob()).then(b=>{
        const el = document.getElementById('live-file-iframe');
        if(el) el.src = URL.createObjectURL(b);
      });
      html += '<div style="margin-top:10px;"><iframe id="live-file-iframe" src="" style="width:100%;height:480px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:4px;"></iframe></div>';
    } else if(type.startsWith('text/')){
      fetch(url).then(r=>r.blob()).then(b=>{
        const el = document.getElementById('live-file-iframe');
        if(el) el.src = URL.createObjectURL(b);
      });
      html += '<div style="margin-top:10px;"><iframe id="live-file-iframe" src="" style="width:100%;height:320px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:4px;background:#fff;"></iframe></div>';
    }
    content.innerHTML = html;
    panel.style.display = 'block';
  }
  async function load(){
    try{
      const r = await fetch(apiBase + '/live-file-info/' + course + '/' + week);
      if(!r.ok){renderFile(null);return;}
      const d = await r.json();
      renderFile(d || null);
    }catch{
      renderFile(null);
    }
  }
  load();
  setInterval(load, 15000);
})();
</script>
